Title: The Last Biscuit
Credit: A radio play by
Author: Lexington's examples

INT. KITCHEN - MORNING

!KITCHEN ATMOS. A CLOCK TICKS. A TIN LID IS PRISED OFF.

ANNA
(close, to herself)
One left. Just one.

!THE BACK DOOR OPENS. BIRDSONG FROM THE GARDEN. BOOTS ON THE MAT.

BRAM
(off, then approaching)
Don't you dare!

ANNA
I was here first.

!THE TIN SLIDES ACROSS THE TABLE.

BRAM
(a struggle)
Give it here...

~Who took the biscuit from the biscuit tin?

> CROSSFADE TO:
